---
// PDF-95 D9. The closing call to action, on the one inverted paper band --
// the last child of `<main>` before `<Footer />`. `PDF-94` removed the
// page's old ending (a second copy of the 31-row licence table) two waves
// earlier and left the page ending on whatever was last; this item gives it
// one on purpose.
//
// Three ranked destinations: the install command itself (primary -- it is
// copyable TEXT, not a link; the action is *type this*), the licence
// inventory (secondary, `/licensing/`, the route `PDF-94` created), source
// on GitHub (tertiary, an already-closed host), and PyPI (the install
// channel itself).
//
// PyPI WAS named and never linked, because `pypi.org` was outside AC12's
// two-host closure. That has been re-ruled: AC12 exists to keep the page
// from FETCHING anything third-party, and a destination a reader clicks is
// not a request the page makes -- `github.com` sat in the closure on
// exactly that footing from the start. `pypi.org` now joins it. The
// property that actually matters is unchanged and still measured: zero
// external requests, at every viewport, on both routes.
//
// The `.on-paper` class (global.css, `PDF-93`) overrides the focus ring to
// `primary-600` on this band -- `primary-400` measures 2.45:1 here and
// fails 3:1. This item is that token's first consumer, not its definer
// (Non-goals: no palette/token/focus-rule definition lives in this diff).
//
// AC20: no version number anywhere in this file, including the closing
// line -- the frontend proposal's own illustrative closing copy (naming the
// public API as of a specific typed release number) is NOT reproduced here
// for exactly that reason; see this item's report for the contradiction
// between that sentence and AC20's own file list, which names this
// component explicitly.
import { withBase } from '../lib/site';
import { langPath, pick } from '../lib/i18n';

const pypiUrl = 'https://pypi.org/project/pdf-tooling/';
const githubUrl = 'https://github.com/ArmandoHerra/pdf-tooling';
const inventoryUrl = withBase(langPath(Astro.url, 'licensing/'));

// The install command itself is NOT in the copy table: it is the one piece
// of text on this band a reader is meant to copy verbatim into a shell,
// and it is the same three words in every language.
const t = pick(Astro.url, {
  eyebrow: 'Get it',
  heading: 'One command, and nothing hidden underneath it',
  lede: 'The same install this page opened with. Copy it, run it, and see the rest for yourself.',
  inventory: 'All packages, with licenses \u2192',
  source: 'Source on GitHub \u2192',
  pypi: 'Also on PyPI \u2192',
  fineprint:
    'Apache-2.0. The structured output shapes and the exit-code table are public API. Bugs and fixes live in GitHub issues and the changelog. Contributions are welcome, under the DCO.',
}, {
  eyebrow: 'Inst\u00e1lala',
  heading: 'Un solo comando, y nada escondido debajo',
  lede: 'La misma instalaci\u00f3n con la que abri\u00f3 esta p\u00e1gina: c\u00f3piala, c\u00f3rrela y comprueba lo dem\u00e1s por tu cuenta.',
  inventory: 'Todos los paquetes, con sus licencias \u2192',
  source: 'C\u00f3digo fuente en GitHub \u2192',
  pypi: 'Tambi\u00e9n en PyPI \u2192',
  fineprint:
    'Apache-2.0. Las formas de salida estructurada y la tabla de c\u00f3digos de salida son API p\u00fablica. Los errores y sus correcciones viven en los issues de GitHub y en el changelog. Las contribuciones son bienvenidas, bajo el DCO.',
});
---

<section class="u-crop on-paper border-t border-line-paper bg-paper-50 py-24 text-surface-900">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 text-center">
    <p class="micro text-primary-700">{t.eyebrow}</p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">
      {t.heading}
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-surface-700">
      {t.lede}
    </p>

    <div
      tabindex="0"
      class="u-selectall mx-auto mt-8 inline-block max-w-full overflow-x-auto rounded-md border border-line-soft bg-surface-950 px-5 py-3.5 text-left font-mono text-sm text-surface-100 shadow-well"
    >
      <code>uv tool install pdf-tooling</code>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-sm font-semibold">
      <!-- `primary-600` (this band's focus-ring override) measures 4.27:1 on
           paper-50 -- FAILS the 4.5:1 body threshold (R7), so it is never
           used as a resting or hover TEXT colour here, only as the focus
           ring. `primary-700` (5.71:1, passes) is the one accent-text shade
           this band uses, at rest and on hover alike. -->
      <a href={inventoryUrl} class="text-primary-700 underline hover:underline-offset-4">
        {t.inventory}
      </a>
      <a href={githubUrl} class="text-primary-700 underline hover:underline-offset-4">
        {t.source}
      </a>
      <a href={pypiUrl} class="text-primary-700 underline hover:underline-offset-4">
        {t.pypi}
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 max-w-xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-surface-600">
      {t.fineprint}
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
